hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"639","Chapter 67: On salam (advance payment). 669 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Najih, from Abdillah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina while they were advancing payment for fruits for two and three years, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advance payment for fruits should be in a known measure to a known term."
"640","670 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Abdillah ibn Kathir, from Abu al-Minhal, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina while they were advancing payment for fruits for two and three years, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Advance payment for fruits should be in a known measure and a known weight."
"641","671 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Mujalid, he said: Abdillah ibn Shaddad and Abu Burdah disputed about salam, so they sent me to Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa and I asked him, and he said: We used to advance payment at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the time of Abu Bakr and the time of Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, for wheat, barley, raisins, and dates, to people who did not have it with them. 672 - He said: Then I asked Ibn Abza, and he said the same."
